  "caption": "Quinn's hallway rug kept trying to catch a toe, midnight loo trips happened in the dark, and getting off the couch took three attempts.\n\nMoving less can weaken the legs, which makes wobbles and falls more likely. Falls prevention usually has two parts: strength and balance work, plus a safer home.\n\nWhat often helps: balance practice about three times a week, sit-to-stands without using your hands, removing trip hazards and adding night lights, and swapping loose slippers for grippy shoes. Getting your eyes and hearing checked can help too.\n\nIf you've had a fall, notice new dizziness or unsteadiness, or fear of falling is holding you back, it's worth getting checked.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
